{
  "schema": "nexloop-ci-stages/1",
  "version": 3,
  "decision": "NX-033 §4.1, ADR-020 §4 baseline exit (owner decision D-j 2026-10-11, 'all as recommended' on the proposal in docs/implementation/NX-033-stages-implementation.md §3; gate limit 5 minutes). As v2, with three changes, all in scripts/ci/check too: (1) the deadline gate (python-deadline-gate) runs the two real-Pi deadline cases and the two Agent Host run-limit cases alone with 4 guard worker processes and the 2 s tool deadline unchanged, at most 300 s (a longer gate is a failed stage); these four are no longer run in the parallel stage; (2) integration-parallel is the former integration stage without the gate cases and the low-parallelism cases (scripts/ci/stages/lib.sh); (3) integration-heavy runs the low-parallelism cases (classes B and C of the baseline that pass serially and time out under the full parallel load) with 2 workers, required as python-heavy; a failure stops the run like any other stage. Baseline rule (the list itself is the dispatcher's, kept outside the repository): a case leaves the baseline after two consecutive full runs pass in its assigned stage; a class C case that fails two consecutive full runs is raised to class B or A; a case with a violation assertion (for example read_assert_memo) is class A on any violation. Test counts move between suites as registered in required-suites.v2.json (count_groups). v1 and v2 are unchanged; the controller uses v3 only when the trusted installation selects it (--stages-version 3).",
  "stages": [
    {
      "name": "dependency-python",
      "network": "dependency",
      "argv": [
        "bash",
        "scripts/ci/stages/dependency-python.sh"
      ],
      "timeout_seconds": 1800
    },
    {
      "name": "static",
      "network": "test",
      "argv": [
        "bash",
        "scripts/ci/stages/static.sh"
      ],
      "timeout_seconds": 900,
      "env": {
        "UV_OFFLINE": "1",
        "npm_config_offline": "true"
      }
    },
    {
